{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4et4FtH5Qwtmb4iY9Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The test fails as expected: `ú` isn't in the hand-written accent table. Here is the full set of root causes I found in `contacts/dedupe.py`:\n\n1. **Accent stripping is a hand-maintained list** (`name_key`, lines 14–15). It only covers 8 letters, so `Ú`, `í`, `ç`, and most others are never folded.\n2. **Decomposed vs. precomposed input (Mac vs. Windows).** macOS often sends `e` + U+0301 while Windows sends `é` (U+00E9). The table only matches the precomposed form, so NFD names never fold. No Unicode normalization is applied.\n3. **`ß` vs. `ss`.** `.lower()` leaves `ß` unchanged; `.casefold()` maps it to `ss`.\n4. **Zero-width/format characters** (e.g. U+200B, U+FEFF, soft hyphen) from copy-paste aren't stripped, and they survive `\\s` matching.\n5. **Transitive matches are lost.** A dropped duplicate's keys are never recorded, so a later record that matches only the dropped one survives. Example: `Anna`/`a@` → `Anna Schmidt`/`a@` (dropped) → `Anna Schmidt`/`b@` (kept, though it's the same person as the second record).\n\nI'll fix these in the library now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13191,"cache_read_input_tokens":25998,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13191},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7c47df0-3509-4ad2-9270-42967be91218","uuid":"da85a269-ab48-42f9-92d6-472a4fe5a171","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:33:04.973Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4esmQHMLBoL1vYTt8T"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4et4FtH5Qwtmb4iY9Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018RffUxWtWKDUTADfLd2wwY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-haiku-5-5-effort-medium-r1/cases/t13_unicode_dedupe/contacts/dedupe.py","content":"import re\nimport unicodedata\n\n_WS = re.compile(r\"\\s+\")\n\n\ndef _fold_marks(s):\n    \"\"\"Decompose (NFKD) and drop combining marks and format characters.\n\n    NFKD makes NFC (Windows) and NFD (macOS) input compare equal, and removing\n    combining marks strips accents for any script, not just a fixed list.\n    Format characters (category Cf) such as zero-width spaces are dropped too.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", s)\n    return \"\".join(c for c in s\n                   if not unicodedata.combining(c) and unicodedata.category(c) != \"Cf\")\n\n\ndef email_key(email):\n    return unicodedata.normalize(\"NFC\", email.strip()).casefold()\n\n\ndef name_key(name):\n    \"\"\"Key for matching names: case-folded, single spaces, no accents.\"\"\"\n    s = _fold_marks(name).casefold()\n    # casefold can introduce marks (e.g. \"İ\" -> \"i\" + U+0307), so fold again\n    s = _fold_marks(s)\n    return _WS.sub(\" \", s).strip()\n\n\ndef dedupe(records):\n    \"\"\"records: list of dicts with 'name' and 'email'. Returns survivors in first-seen order.\n\n    A record is dropped if its name or email key matches any earlier record,\n    including records that were themselves dropped. Matching is therefore\n    transitive, so each record's keys are added to the seen set either way.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen, out = set(), []\n    for r in records:\n        keys = {(\"name\", name_key(r[\"name\"])), (\"email\", email_key(r[\"email\"]))}\n        if not keys & seen:\n            out.append(r)\n        seen |= keys\n    return out\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13191,"cache_read_input_tokens":25998,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13191},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7c47df0-3509-4ad2-9270-42967be91218","uuid":"afbc7163-193b-40d7-8198-1b17c8ab7cc2","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:33:07.259Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4esmQHMLBoL1vYTt8T","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018RffUxWtWKDUTADfLd2wwY":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-haiku-5-5-effort-medium-r1/cases/t13_unicode_dedupe/contacts/dedupe.py","content":"import re\nimport unicodedata\n\n_WS = re.compile(r\"\\s+\")\n\n\ndef _fold_marks(s):\n    \"\"\"Decompose (NFKD) and drop combining marks and format characters.\n\n    NFKD makes NFC (Windows) and NFD (macOS) input compare equal, and removing\n    combining marks strips accents for any script, not just a fixed list.\n    Format characters (category Cf) such as zero-width spaces are dropped too.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", s)\n    return \"\".join(c for c in s\n                   if not unicodedata.combining(c) and unicodedata.category(c) != \"Cf\")\n\n\ndef email_key(email):\n    return unicodedata.normalize(\"NFC\", email.strip()).casefold()\n\n\ndef name_key(name):\n    \"\"\"Key for matching names: case-folded, single spaces, no accents.\"\"\"\n    s = _fold_marks(name).casefold()\n    # casefold can introduce marks (e.g. \"İ\" -> \"i\" + U+0307), so fold again\n    s = _fold_marks(s)\n    return _WS.sub(\" \", s).strip()\n\n\ndef dedupe(records):\n    \"\"\"records: list of dicts with 'name' and 'email'. Returns survivors in first-seen order.\n\n    A record is dropped if its name or email key matches any earlier record,\n    including records that were themselves dropped. Matching is therefore\n    transitive, so each record's keys are added to the seen set either way.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen, out = set(), []\n    for r in records:\n        keys = {(\"name\", name_key(r[\"name\"])), (\"email\", email_key(r[\"email\"]))}\n        if not keys & seen:\n            out.append(r)\n        seen |= keys\n    return out\n"}}}
