{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4fyiMbS1WGpDz9B4LB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`tests/test_dedupe.py` now passes (1 passed). The fix is in `contacts/dedupe.py`, and I didn't touch the test. The change is uncommitted.\n\n**Root causes and fixes**\n\n1. **Accent stripping used a hand-written list of 8 letters.** `Ú`, `í`, `ç` and most others were never folded, which is what the reproduction hits. Accents are now removed with Unicode decomposition (NFKD) plus dropping combining marks, so any script works.\n2. **Mac vs. Windows encodings.** macOS often sends `e` + combining accent (NFD) and Windows sends a single precomposed character (NFC). The old list only matched the precomposed form. NFKD makes both compare equal. Emails also get NFC before casefolding.\n3. **`ß` vs. `ss`.** `.lower()` leaves `ß` alone. Keys now use `.casefold()`, which maps `ß` to `ss`.\n4. **Invisible characters from copy-paste** (zero-width space, BOM, soft hyphen) were not stripped, so they broke matches. Format characters (Unicode category Cf) are now dropped.\n5. **Lost transitive matches.** A dropped duplicate's keys were never recorded, so a later record that matched only the dropped one survived. Example: `Anna`/`a@`, then `Anna Schmidt`/`a@` (dropped), then `Anna Schmidt`/`b@`, which previously survived. `dedupe` now adds each record's keys to the seen set whether or not it is kept.\n\nThe first-seen record is still the survivor.\n\n**Checks I ran:** the reproduction test, plus ad hoc checks for NFD vs. NFC names, `ß`/`ss`, zero-width characters, mixed-case email, the transitive chain, and that distinct names (`Ana` vs. `Anna`) stay separate. All behaved as expected.\n\n**Decisions for you to review**\n\n- Change 5 changes behavior beyond the three reported symptoms: matching is now transitive. If you want strictly pairwise matching, tell me and I'll revert that part.\n- I did not add `ü` → `ue` folding. The spec only covers `ß` vs. `ss`, so `Müller` and `Mueller` still don't match.\n\nI also restored a tracked `.pyc` file that my test run regenerated, so the diff is only `contacts/dedupe.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3660,"cache_read_input_tokens":47576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3660},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7c47df0-3509-4ad2-9270-42967be91218","uuid":"5e534e5a-dd3c-4a4f-ab1f-92687a9d0932","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:33:21.211Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4fyRzDvT1NWYH17TUM"}
